I am continuing this canonical PR for the confirmed registry-discovery gap in #140620 under maintainer landing authority. The reporter now confirms that primary transcripts exceeded the legacy registry and that extending the registry before migration increased the import from230 to634. Trajectory envelopes are explicitly not primary transcripts.

@leochun92-sudo, I plan to retain your diagnosis and credit while moving the repair to the current Doctor Session SQLite migration owner. The retired orphan classifier and synchronous generic path scan will not be carried forward. Scope is validated historical primary discovery, current-owner preservation, manifest-backed recovery, and before/after search and no-loss proof. No runtime filesystem fallback, diagnostic-trajectory conversion, or relaxed cleanup eligibility.

Existing references and already-owned SQLite windows take precedence. Unregistered primary files need validated transcript identity and an unambiguous owning agent; shared/unverifiable inputs remain protected. The implementation and proof will stay on this PR, not a duplicate.
